error[consumed_borrowed_handle]: `g5_close` ends the life of what it is given, and `a` was borrowed — this function promised not to change it
  at tests/golden/full/fixedbugs-2242-a-wrapper-ending-its-borrowed-handle-is-told-where-the-at-goes.hero:22:21
     |
  22 |     return g5_close(a)  #~ consumed_borrowed_handle
     |                     ^
  note: a parameter written without `@` is borrowed: the caller keeps the value and reads it again after the call, so a call that frees it leaves them holding an address C has taken back. Write the parameter `@a` in the signature of `done` and `@` before its argument at every call of `done`, which says on both lines that the value does not survive; this call stays as it is, since `g5_close` takes this argument without `@`
  note: this refuses the call, not the copy: a copy made BEFORE the call still holds the freed address, and nothing here sees that. design.md Part 8 wart 20 states that cost and names what would close it
